  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x200b;&#x200b;Emergency Movement and Relocation Assistance for Refugees in Benishangul-Gumuz Region of Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ethiopia has a long-standing history of receiving refugees and is currently the third-largest refugee hosting country in Africa and one of the largest refugee asylum countries worldwide, reflecting the ongoing fragility and conflict in the East and Horn of Africa region. Among the principal factors for this include political turmoil, conflict and drought in Sudan, South Sudan and Somalia. In coordination with the Government of Ethiopia&#x2019;s Refugee and Returnee Service, the UN Refugee Agency (UNHCR), and other humanitarian partners, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is one of the main humanitarian agencies providing movement assistance and relocation assistance to vulnerable refugees from border entry points to the safety of camps and inter-camps. Through this project, with funding from UNHCR, IOM is assisting 14,000 refugees affected by the conflict in Sudan who arrived in Benishangul Gumuz region with timely, safe and dignified emergency movement assistance services and relocation assistance from entry points to designated camps. Over a four-month period, IOM is providing assistance that includes include pre-embarkation health checks, and safe and dignified movement assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
